<newsitem itemid="254531" id="root" date="1996-12-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Monex returns to profit, mulls rights offer.</title>
<headline>Monex returns to profit, mulls rights offer.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     none	  vs 6.0 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   0.01	  vs 1.82 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.71	  vs 2.47 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.30	  vs 0.65</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.51	  vs 0.37</p>
<p>    Turnover		  16.52	 vs 15.17</p>
<p>Full name: Monex Ltd (formerly Ilco Homes)</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the housing and construction divisions were expected to perform at current levels for the rest of the year, and the brick division to improve its performance. They said Monex planned to diversify into the leisure industry.</p>
<p>They said the company planned to hold a rights offer in March 1997 in order for it to take full advantage of the Century City development which is expected to open at the end of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
